<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alaeddin Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1398">1398</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Alâeddin Ali Bey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alaeddin Bey was ruler of the Karamanids in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> from about 1361. Though married to a daughter of the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-i">Murad I</a>, he repeatedly fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, who defeated him in 1386 and again at Akçay in 1397, after which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayezid-i">Bayezid I</a> had him executed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a> restored the dynasty in 1402.</p></div>
